data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"filePath\": \"/tmp/dev-dispatch.md\", \"content\": \"# Task: greet, tested\\n\\nImplement the following in your clone of the subject repository, commit it to\\nyour own branch, and reply. Do not touch anything outside these two files.\\n\\n## 1. src/greet.py\\n\\nCreate `src/greet.py` (create the `src/` directory if needed) containing a\\nfunction:\\n\\n    def greet(name):\\n        return \\\"Hello, \\\" + name + \\\"!\\\"\\n\\nRequirements:\\n- `greet(name)` returns exactly the string `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` — e.g.\\n  `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`.\\n- `greet(\\\"\\\")` returns exactly `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`.\\n- No other behavior is required; keep it simple.\\n\\n## 2. tests/test_greet.py\\n\\nCreate `tests/test_greet.py` (create the `tests/` directory if needed) with\\n`unittest` tests covering at least:\\n- a normal name, e.g. asserting `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`;\\n- the empty string, e.g. asserting `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`.\\n\\nMake the import of `greet` work when tests are run from the repository root\\nwith the command below (e.g. via `sys.path` insertion of `src/`, or\\n`sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \\\"..\\\", \\\"src\\\"))` —\\nyour choice, as long as it works).\\n\\n## 3. Verify\\n\\nFrom the repository root run exactly:\\n\\n    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n\\nIt must exit 0. Run it yourself and confirm before replying.\\n\\n## 4. Commit and reply\\n\\n- Commit both files to your own branch (the one your clone is on) before\\n  replying — an uncommitted change does not survive.\\n- Reply with a summary stating: the files created, the exact unittest command\\n  you ran, and its exit code. Tell the truth: I will fetch your branch and\\n  run the command myself to judge the work.\\n\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_13","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1788418240,"id":"chatcmpl-aaf63a48039a418aabc82a75f00b491e","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

